   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Types of home and rooms",
     "texto": [
      "In Norwegian, the indefinite articles **en** and **et** come before the noun: **en leilighet**, **et hus**. In Bokmål, many feminine words also take the common-gender article **en**.",
      "For the definite form, the article is added at the end: et hus → huset; en leilighet → leiligheten. In English «the» comes in front of the noun; in Norwegian it is usually attached to the end of the noun.",
      "As a pronoun, **den** means «it» or «that» and refers back to a common-gender noun, such as **leilighet**. **Det** is used with neuter nouns."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
